Incidentally, I've been playing a wizard whose only attack spells are
force bolt and fireball. Casting light has become a more or less
automatic foreplay.

I see several ways to shed light at a distance (provided you've not
run out of light sources)
- cast the spell
- zap a wand of light
- read a scroll of light
- throw a lit candle
- throw a lit lantern
- throw a lit lamp
The last three might be an option for a valkyrie in Gehennom, where
plenty of walls will conveniently stop the thrown lights.

By the way, the spoiler spl-343 (Hugo, O'Donell) is wrong about
fireball and cone of cold:
"2 to 9 explosions follow; the first is centred at the location you
chose, subsequent ones randomly at any of the nine squares around that
point "
There's only 8 squares around a given center, and I've been positively
hit by fireballs cast by me at distance 2.

